content:
emma: Customer (Acme) reports our API returns a schema validation error when proxying OpenAI-compatible tool calls. They say the tool response is valid per the model, but our gateway throws: "validation failed: unexpected field 'args'". Repro attached.

support-bot: Ticket created #INC-2026-1789 (linked to Acme account). :ticket:

raj: can you paste the exact request/response pair? need headers + body.

emma: here — stripped sensitive bits.
```http
POST /v1/responses
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer REDACTED

{
  "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
  "input": "Call the payment API",
  "functions": [
    {
      "name": "create_payment",
      "description": "Create a payment",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "amount": {"type": "number"},
          "currency": {"type": "string", "enum": ["usd","eur"]},
          "priority": {"type": "string", "enum": ["low","medium","high"]}
        },
        "required": ["amount","currency"]
      }
    }
  ],
  "response": {
    "content": "",
    "tool_call": {
      "name": "create_payment",
      "args": "{\"amount\": 123.45, \"currency\": \"USD\", \"priority\": \"High\"}"
    }
  }
}
```

maria: aha — two things jump out:
- They are returning the tool args as a string (`args` stringified JSON) instead of an object (`arguments` or `args` as object) — our validator expects an object.
- Enum case mismatch: our schema uses lowercase `usd`/`eur` and `low`/`medium`/`high`, but the tool sent `USD` and `High`. Our strict enum check fails.

oncall: do we follow OpenAI tool calling canonical names? there are a few flavors in the wild. we currently enforce: `tool_call.arguments` (object) or `tool_call.args` (object) and enums must match exactly.

raj: customer says OpenAI-compatible models sometimes stringify args (older SDKs) and sometimes use `arguments` vs `args`. We should accept both shapes for compatibility.

maria: quick repro I ran locally shows our validator error: 
```
ValidationError: tool_call.args must be an object
at validateToolCall (/srv/runtime/validators.js:142:15)
at handleResponse (/srv/runtime/handler.js:88:10)
```

emma: customer workaround: ask model to return `tool_call.arguments` as an object and normalize enums to lowercase — but they can't control 3rd-party model variants. need server-side fix.

oncall: proposed mitigation plan (short term):
- Accept stringified JSON for `tool_call.args` and attempt JSON.parse with safe fallback.
- Accept `tool_call.arguments` as an alias for `tool_call.args`.
- Make enum comparison case-insensitive for common fields (currency, priority) or try to coerce to lowercase before validation, but only for listed safe keys.

maria: agree. caveat: coercing enums could mask real semantic differences in some schemas. let's restrict coercion to specific AWS-like enums: currency, locale, priority, status — documented list.

raj: can we ship a compatibility patch to staging today? customer on enterprise plan, hitting production errors.

oncall: i can push a non-breaking middleware by EOD to staging: it will:
1) If `tool_call.args` is a string, attempt JSON.parse.
2) If `tool_call.arguments` exists and `tool_call.args` missing, copy arguments -> args.
3) For fields in SAFE_ENUM_KEYS = ["currency","priority","status","level"], if value is string, set value = value.toLowerCase() before schema validation.

I'll run quick unit tests and smoke on staging.

support-bot: @emma updated ticket INC-2026-1789 with mitigation plan & ETA (staging patch by EOD).

emma: sample compatibility shim I used locally for tests:
```js
function normalizeToolCallTool(tool_call) {
  if (!tool_call) return tool_call;
  if (tool_call.arguments && !tool_call.args) {
    tool_call.args = tool_call.arguments;
  }
  if (typeof tool_call.args === 'string') {
    try { tool_call.args = JSON.parse(tool_call.args); } catch (e) { /* leave as-is and fail later */ }
  }
  const SAFE_ENUM_KEYS = ['currency','priority','status','level'];
  SAFE_ENUM_KEYS.forEach(k => {
    if (tool_call.args && typeof tool_call.args[k] === 'string') {
      tool_call.args[k] = tool_call.args[k].toLowerCase();
    }
  });
  return tool_call;
}
```

maria: looks good. also add logging for detected coercions so we can later add telemetry and follow up with partners who keep sending uppercase enums.

oncall: will add a feature-flag gate and telemetry tag `compat:openai_toolcall_mappings` so we can toggle and roll back quickly.

raj: can you capture exact model output that triggered this? we should link the original model response in the ticket.

emma: pasted the customer's model response in ticket notes. they said model is 3rd-party fork and probably older.

maria: next steps for eng-runtime (owners):
- Add middleware + unit tests (maria)
- Smoke staging and run customer repro (oncall)
- If green, schedule hotfix to prod with feature-flag on (oncall)
- Postmortem note + docs update to explain our compatibility behavior (raj)

oncall: ETA: patch to staging in 2h, deploy to prod if smoke OK in 6h.

raj: told customer workarounds and ETA, they acknowledged. :thumbsup:

support-bot: INC-2026-1789 status -> in_progress (assigned to maria, oncall).

emma: thanks all — please @mention me when prod patch is live so I can confirm with Acme.

maria: patch merged to staging, running tests now. added telemetry events for `compat_coerce` and `compat_parsed_string_args`.

oncall: staging smoke passed. deploying to prod now behind feature flag.

ticketing-bot: INC-2026-1789 updated: prod deployment complete (flag=on).

emma: I confirmed with Acme — they no longer see validation errors. closing from our side once we monitor for 24h.

raj: creating follow-up card to add a short section in the docs: "OpenAI-compatible tool calling variants we normalize".

maria: created PR for docs and linked it in the ticket.

emma: closing thread here. thanks! :white_check_mark:
